<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wat Phra That Lampang Luang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wat Phra That Lampang Luang is a Buddhist temple near Lampang in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, built within a walled enclosure on an old fortified mound. Its large gilded chedi, said to enshrine a relic of the Buddha, and its wooden open-sided halls make it one of the finest examples of Lanna architecture. Local tradition links it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nan-thip-chang">Nan Thip Chang</a>'s defeat of the Burmese governor of Lampang in 1732.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wat-phra-that-lampang-luang.jpg" alt="Wat Phra That Lampang Luang" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hong2101 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%B1%E0%B8%94%E0%B8%9E%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%B0%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%B3%E0%B8%9B%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%87%E0%B8%AB%E0%B8%A5%E0%B8%A7%E0%B8%87_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
